The Cellular settings Interface
•	The interface is visually organized into three principal areas: the status area, the navigation/header area, and the content area:
o	Status Bar: Spanning the uppermost portion of the display from left to right:
	Time: Displays the local time as 12:46. Positioned to its right is the silent mode icon.
	Dynamic Island: The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator.
	Connectivity & Power: The Airplane Mode icon denotes that wireless network transmissions are currently disabled. The adjacent battery icon is partially filled, displaying the numeric charge level 1 centered within the housing.
o	Navigation & Header Bar: Establishing the user's hierarchical location within the iOS environment:
	Back-Navigation: The upper-left margin displays a back-navigation link labeled "Settings" accompanied by a directional chevron.
o	Interface Body:
	Introductory Module: Positioned at the upper portion of the viewport immediately below the navigation bar, presenting an introductory visual block composed of the following elements:
•	Icon Graphic: A solid green rounded square containing a wireless transmission symbol.
•	Primary Heading: Centrally aligned or positioned directly adjacent, rendered in bold typography: "Cellular".
•	Descriptive Text: Find out how much data you're using, set data restrictions, and manage carrier settings such as eSIM and Wi-Fi calling. Learn more...".
	Visible Controls & Status Indicators (Initial View): Positioned immediately below the Introductory Module:
•	First group of settings:
o	Cellular Data:  Toggled Off (gray).
o	Cellular Data Options: Displays the status "Roaming On."
o	Personal Hotspot: Displays the status "Off", and appears grayed out, which indicates it is disabled, meaning, it cannot be controlled by the user.
o	Explicative text under these settings: Turn off cellular data to restrict all data to Wi-Fi, including email, web browsing, and push notifications.
•	Under the VERIZON module:
o	Turn On This Line:  Toggled On (green).
o	My Number: +1 (669) 326-4200
o	Wi-Fi Calling: Displays the status “Off.”
o	Carrier Services: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
o	SIM PIN: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
o	Delete eSIM: red colored letters
